# @APP_NAME@ @VERSION@

@APP_NAME@ is a free, open-source (MIT) Mac app that records your meetings, transcribes them live, and gives you a real-time copilot. It sends no telemetry. Live transcription and the assistant use providers you choose and pay for yourself.

## What is new

@HIGHLIGHTS@

## Requirements

- macOS 14 (Sonoma) or later.
- Apple Silicon (arm64). There is no Intel build.
- A [Soniox](https://console.soniox.com) API key for live transcription. Soniox is a hosted service, so recorded audio leaves your Mac for it.
- A key for one assistant provider: DeepSeek, OpenAI or OpenRouter.

## Install

Download `@DMG_NAME@`, open it, and drag @APP_NAME@ to Applications.

@FIRST_OPEN@

## Permissions

macOS asks for these the first time a feature needs them: Microphone, System Audio Recording, Screen Recording, Calendars and Notifications. Launch at Login is an option in Settings, and macOS may refuse it for an ad hoc build.

